body:
@jorge-lip Thanks for merging my fix for the overriding of HOME.

As for the banner: I don't mind if it is there, but the [CWL reference runner](https://github.com/common-workflow-language/cwltool) is trying to use `udocker` as a drop-in replacement for `docker`, so it would be best if `docker`'s behavior was matched in this regard.

Otherwise we would add more special code just for `udocker`. Either way I don't think it is a good idea to mix diagnostic messages with output from the container in the same output stream — that's the whole point of STDERR :-)

Thanks for being so fast!

@mr-c gave me a solution, forcing docker to use a particular user in the container, like this:

`docker run --user ${USER} --rm --volume=$PWD:/tmp/workdir -w=/tmp/workdir me/cwltool-udocker cwltool --user-space-docker-cmd=udocker pack/pack.cwl pack/jobs/lab-mod.yml`

@jorge-lip thanks for the response, I tried running udocer inside both an ubuntu and an alpine container, both cases secoomp denies getting a shell, this is the error: 
```
proot error: ptrace(TRACEME): Operation not permitted
proot error: execve("/bin/terraform"): Operation not permitted
proot info: possible causes:
* the program is a script but its interpreter (eg. /bin/sh) was not found;
* the program is an ELF but its interpreter (eg. ld-linux.so) was not found;
* the program is a foreign binary but qemu was not specified;
* qemu does not work correctly (if specified);
* the loader was not found or doesn't work.
fatal error: see `proot-x86_64-4_8_0 --help`.
proot error: can't chmod '/tmp/proot-4868-mf2sRh': No such file or directory
```

I was able to get it running in ubuntu by starting the container with unconfined seccomp, thus disabling all features of seccomp, will it be possible to provide the requires seccomp profiles only or am I missing something

